From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kernel32: a mailslot can be given to a completion port

Opera's installer creates a mailslot for its backend's messages and gives
it to an I/O completion port, CHECKing that it worked; it stopped there
with a breakpoint exception (0x80000003) and Opera was never installed
(the Store walk, 2026-10-01). CreateMailslot made the mailslot synchronous
(FILE_SYNCHRONOUS_IO_NONALERT), and wineserver refuses a synchronous
handle to a completion port. Windows' CreateMailslot does not make it
synchronous; ReadFile still waits for a caller without an OVERLAPPED.

Test: test/mailslot-gate.sh with test/mailslot-probe.c (mutant
SG_MUTANT_MAILSLOT_SYNC). Opera 136's installer now installs opera.exe.
---
--- a/dlls/kernel32/sync.c
+++ b/dlls/kernel32/sync.c
@@ -692,8 +692,17 @@
     else
         timeout.QuadPart = ((LONGLONG)0x7fffffff << 32) | 0xffffffff;
 
+    /* Stained Glass OS: not synchronous, as Windows' -- a program may give
+     * the mailslot to an I/O completion port (Opera's installer does, and
+     * stopped when the port was refused); ReadFile still waits for a
+     * caller without an OVERLAPPED */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_MAILSLOT_SYNC
+    if (!set_ntstatus( NtCreateMailslotFile( &handle, GENERIC_READ | SYNCHRONIZE, &attr, &iosb,
+                                             FILE_WRITE_THROUGH, 0, nMaxMessageSize, &timeout )))
+#else
     if (!set_ntstatus( NtCreateMailslotFile( &handle, GENERIC_READ | SYNCHRONIZE, &attr, &iosb,
                                              FILE_SYNCHRONOUS_IO_NONALERT, 0, nMaxMessageSize, &timeout )))
+#endif
         handle = INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE;
 
     RtlFreeUnicodeString( &nameW );
